        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: камень",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "камень (kámen) — \"a stone\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "камень (kámen) from Proto-Slavic kamy, with the stem kamen- — inherited. Vasmer relates it to Old Norse hamarr, \"hammer\", so English hammer is a cousin, beside Lithuanian akmuõ and Greek ákmōn, \"anvil\", from a related form."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
